target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsTheRecordRatherThanBeingTold'
expect: an absent run derived
why:    convergence is READ FROM THE RECORD, never asserted — it used to arrive as `--clean-exit`, a bare flag, so the one question the gate exists to answer was answered by the orchestrator asserting it. A run id absent from the store is UNKNOWN: there is no record to read, which is not the same as converged, and absence is the cheapest thing to produce.
--- old
	res := Result{Push: push, Reason: reason, Convergence: conv}
--- new
	if runs[p.RunID] == nil {
		conv = record.Converged
	}
	res := Result{Push: push, Reason: reason, Convergence: conv}
